# Digest-bearing contract files: their SHA-256 is computed over the checked-in
# bytes (compile-time include_str! / include_bytes!), so the checkout must
# deliver identical bytes on every platform. Without this, Windows autocrlf
# rewrites LF to CRLF and every baked digest check fails as tampered.
crates/synapse-module/owned-decode-manifests/** text eol=lf
bench/campaign/*-fixtures/** text eol=lf
bench/fixtures/** text eol=lf
evidence/** text eol=lf

# Parsed by structure at compile time (include_str!): the drift-guard tests
# find the operation inventory by its blank-line paragraph break, which a CRLF
# checkout turns into \r\n\r\n.
docs/wire-contract-v1.md text eol=lf
